A bag contains $7$ red and $5$ black counters.
Two counters are taken out one after the other, and the first counter is **not** replaced.
On the probability tree, $R$ means red and $B$ means black.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N1) at (2.2,1.4);
\coordinate (N2) at (2.2,-1.4);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,0.7);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,-0.7);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O) -- (N1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{7}{12}$};
\draw (O) -- (N2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{5}{12}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$b$};
\draw (N1) -- (E2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$a$};
\draw (N2) -- (E3) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{7}{11}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E4) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{4}{11}$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N1) {$R$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N2) {$B$};
\node[right] at (E1) {$R$};
\node[right] at (E2) {$B$};
\node[right] at (E3) {$R$};
\node[right] at (E4) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which fraction belongs at $a$?

A bag contains $4$ red and $5$ blue marbles.
Two marbles are taken out without replacement, where $R$ means red and $B$ means blue.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (N1) at (2.2,1.4);
\coordinate (N2) at (2.2,-1.4);
\coordinate (E1) at (4.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E2) at (4.8,0.7);
\coordinate (E3) at (4.8,-0.7);
\coordinate (E4) at (4.8,-2.4);
\draw (O) -- (N1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{4}{9}$};
\draw (O) -- (N2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{5}{9}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E1) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{3}{8}$};
\draw (N1) -- (E2) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{5}{8}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E3) node[midway, above, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{4}{8}$};
\draw (N2) -- (E4) node[midway, below, fill=white, font=\small] {$\frac{4}{8}$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N1) {$R$};
\node[fill=white, inner sep=2pt] at (N2) {$B$};
\node[right] at (E1) {$R$};
\node[right] at (E2) {$B$};
\node[right] at (E3) {$R$};
\node[right] at (E4) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the probability that both marbles are red?

